{"id":"geregelt","lemma":"geregelt","pos":"adj","rank":3451,"glosses":["regulated"],"audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/cf/De-geregelt.ogg/De-geregelt.ogg.mp3","forms":{"comparative":"geregelter","superlative":"am geregeltsten"},"examples":[{"text":"Das Problem ist noch nicht geregelt.","en":"The problem isn't settled yet.","words":[{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"problem"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},null,null,null],"phrases":[[3,5,"not yet"]]},{"text":"Ein Reisebüro hat alles für unsere Reise geregelt.","en":"A travel agent arranged everything for our trip.","words":[{"g":"a"},{"g":"travel agency"},{"g":"has","l":"haben"},{"g":"everything"},{"g":"for"},{"g":"our","l":"unser"},{"g":"journey, travel"},null]},{"text":"Tom hat die Situation geregelt.","en":"Tom took care of the situation.","words":[null,{"g":"has","l":"haben"},{"g":"the"},{"g":"situation"},null]},{"text":"Die Angelegenheit ist vollständig geregelt.","en":"The matter is all settled.","words":[{"g":"the"},{"g":"matter, issue, affair"},{"g":"is","l":"sein"},{"g":"complete"},null]},{"text":"Diese Angelegenheit muss über kurz oder lang geregelt werden.","en":"This matter must be dealt with sooner or later.","words":[{"g":"this one, this","l":"dieser"},{"g":"matter, issue, affair"},{"g":"to have to","l":"müssen"},{"g":"[with accusative or…"},{"g":"short, quick, brief"},{"g":"or"},{"g":"long"},null,{"g":"to become"}]}]}